WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:06.481
Is Text All You Need? Text as a universal
information bottleneck for speech LLMs.

00:00:08.081 --> 00:00:13.009
A speech LLM needs a bridge from the
speech encoder into the language model.

00:00:13.309 --> 00:00:17.683
Learned adapters can place speech
anywhere, even where no text token lives.

00:00:17.983 --> 00:00:23.167
Transcript objectives keep what was said,
but emotion also depends on how it was said.

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:26.112
Can the model's own text embeddings carry both?

00:00:27.512 --> 00:00:29.372
For every speech frame,

00:00:29.372 --> 00:00:36.003
C-Gate scores all 152,064 rows of the
frozen embedding table and keeps the top 16.

00:00:36.303 --> 00:00:41.017
It mixes those original rows with weights
that are non-negative and sum to one.

00:00:41.317 --> 00:00:45.072
So the bridge never leaves the
convex hull of text embeddings.

00:00:46.572 --> 00:00:55.319
Whisper encodes, Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct decodes, and
only 8.6 percent of the parameters are trained.

00:01:00.052 --> 00:01:05.577
The same decoder transcribes and recognises
emotion. Only the instruction changes.

00:01:07.077 --> 00:01:13.648
With our training, C-Gate reaches a 3.98 percent
word error rate on LibriSpeech test-clean,

00:01:13.948 --> 00:01:16.977
and 84.3 percent emotion accuracy.

00:01:18.877 --> 00:01:23.485
One frozen text vocabulary carries
both what was said and how it was said.
